{"availability":"available","full":"paulocdf/digital-memory","name":"digital-memory","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2022-04-23T19:26:46Z","updated":"2026-05-07T08:17:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://paulocdf.github.io/digital-memory","topics":[],"demo":"https://paulocdf.github.io/digital-memory","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T23:19:13.081Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T23:19:13.081Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T23:19:13.081Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T23:19:13.081Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A personal knowledge management system — connecting ideas, books, and notes. Built as a local-first web application on top of Hugo, with IndexedDB as the primary data store and optional Firestore cloud sync.","Digital Memory is a self-hosted digital garden that combines note-taking, task management, spaced repetition, and analytics into a single client-side application. All 40,000 lines of JavaScript run directly in the browser with no server-side logic — data lives in IndexedDB first, with Firebase providing authentication and cloud sync."],"features":["Notes & Sections — Organized into Books, Topics, Snippets, and Inbox. Markdown editor with toolbar and live preview, wikilinks ([[Note Title]]), backlinks, note pinning, and tag cloud.","Knowledge Graph — D3.js force-directed graph on the landing page. Nodes represent notes; edges are derived from wikilinks and title mentions.","Full-Text Search — FlexSearch-powered search indexed from IndexedDB, with keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl/Cmd+K).","Version History — LCS diff viewer with restore and delete support, up to 50 versions per note.","Diagrams — Mermaid and Kroki (PlantUML, D2, GraphViz) rendering with fullscreen lightbox."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/paulocdf/digital-memory/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint"